Polymorphism means one method name having different behaviors. In Java, it allows the same method to perform different tasks based on context.

Example:
class Demo {
 void show() {
 System.out.println("No parameters");
 }
 void show(int a) {
 System.out.println(a);
 }
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 Demo d = new Demo();
 d.show();
 d.show(10);
 }
}

This is called method overloading.

Method overriding occurs when a child class provides its own implementation of a parent class method. Dynamic binding decides which method to call at runtime.

Example:
class Parent {
 void show() {
 System.out.println("Parent show");
 }
}
class Child extends Parent {
 void show() {
 System.out.println("Child show");
 }
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 Parent p = new Child();
 p.show();
 }
}

The method call is resolved at runtime.

Java में polymorphism का मतलब है एक method का अलग-अलग तरीकों से काम करना। यह method overloading और method overriding से होता है।

Example:
class Test {
